@hostname = localhost
@port = 5117
@host = http://{{hostname}}:{{port}}

### Test Case 1: Fetch Diagnostic Operational Heartbeat Status
# Expected Result: HTTP 200 OK | Plain text verification payload string.
GET {{host}}/system
Accept: application/json

###

### Test Case 2: Fetch Current Available Literature Stock (Initially Empty)
# Expected Result: HTTP 200 OK | Raw JSON Array [].
GET {{host}}/books/available
Accept: application/json

###

### Test Case 3: Insert Book Asset 1 (Clean Architecture Manual)
# Expected Result: HTTP 201 Created | Complete JSON body echoing generated ID 1.
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "title": "Clean Architecture",
    "author": "Robert C. Martin",
    "category": "Software Engineering",
    "description": "A craftsman's guide to software structure and design."
}

###

### Test Case 4: Insert Book Asset 2 (Test-Driven Development Guide)
# Expected Result: HTTP 201 Created | Complete JSON body echoing generated ID 2.
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "title": "Test-Driven Development",
    "author": "Kent Beck",
    "category": "Agile Practices",
    "description": "By example methodology breakdown."
}

###

### Test Case 5: Re-Fetch Available Stock (Confirming Catalog Additions)
# Expected Result: HTTP 200 OK | JSON Array populated with Book objects 1 and 2.
GET {{host}}/books/available
Accept: application/json

###

### Test Case 6: Input Field Data Validation Check (Deliberate Empty Title)
# Expected Result: HTTP 400 Bad Request | Explicit text error response warning.
POST {{host}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "",
    "author": "Martin Fowler",
    "category": "Refactoring Architecture"
}

###
### Test Case 7: Execute Book Checkout Workflow (Issue Asset 1 to Member 1)
# Expected Result: HTTP 200 OK | Success message token, matching TransactionId, and calculated +14 day due date.
POST {{host}}/transactions/issue
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "bookId": 1,
    "memberId": 1
}

###

### Test Case 8: Concurrency/Availability Check (Attempt to Double-Issue Asset 1)
# Expected Result: HTTP 400 Bad Request | "The requested book catalog asset is currently unavailable for loan."
POST {{host}}/transactions/issue
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "bookId": 1,
    "memberId": 1
}

###

### Test Case 9: Confirm Stock Reduction (Asset 1 should be omitted from available views)
# Expected Result: HTTP 200 OK | JSON Array showing ONLY Book 2 ("Test-Driven Development").
GET {{host}}/books/available
Accept: application/json

###

### Test Case 10: Execute Book Check-In Return Workflow (Release Asset 1)
# Expected Result: HTTP 200 OK | "Book returned and inventory updated successfully."
POST {{host}}/transactions/return
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "bookId": 1,
    "memberId": 1
}

###

### Test Case 11: Idempotency Return Check (Attempting to re-return already shelved book)
# Expected Result: HTTP 404 Not Found | "No active tracking transaction record found for this explicit Book-Member pair."
POST {{host}}/transactions/return
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "bookId": 1,
    "memberId": 1
}

###

### Test Case 12: Confirm Complete Inventory Inventory Reset
# Expected Result: HTTP 200 OK | JSON Array displaying both Book 1 and Book 2 safely back on the shelves.
GET {{host}}/books/available
Accept: application/json